16. Check After changing the disk partiton table :

   Command : partprob

   partprobe tells the Linux kernel to re-read the partition table after you create, delete, or modify partitions.

   Refresh the kernel's partition information.
   Detect newly created or modified partitions.
   Avoid rebooting after partition changes

  syntax : partprobe /dev/nvme0n1

17. parted

   parted is linux disk parition utility used to create, delete, modify, resize and manage paritions on both MBR (DOS) and GPT disks

   Command : parted

   then after (parted): print

   print : it displays the Disk Name, Disk Size, Partition table type(msdos and gpt), Existing partitions,Start and End Partitions, File system type, Flags

18. Fourth End Filesystem :

   Command : mkfs.ext4

   Example : mkfs.ext4 /dev/ext4-vg/ext4-lv

   mkfs.ext4 creates an EXT4 filesystem on a partition, making it ready to store files and directories.



19. volume group :

   volume group is pool created by combining one or more physical volumes

   Command : vgcreate

   Example : vgcreate devops-vg /dev/nvme0n1p3
   
  verify : vgs

20 . Logical volume 

   lvcreate creates a Logical Volume from the available storage in a Volume Group. The Logical Volume can then be formatted with a filesystem and mounted for storing data.

   command : lvcreate 

   Example : lvcreate -L 1G -n data-lv devops-vg

   verify  : lvs

   lvcreate --> creates logical volume

   -L 1G   --> LV Size = 1GB

   -n data-lv --> Logical Volume Name

   devops -vg --> Take storage from vg

21. Detailed Information Logical volumes

    command : lvdisplay

22. lvextend increases the size of an existing LVM Logical Volume using free space available in its Volume Group

     Command : lvextend

     Example : lvextend -L +500M /dev/devops-vg/data-lv

     Differnece : -L 500  - > set total lv size is 500
                  +500    - > ADD Another 500mb


23. xfs_growfs expands an XFS filesystem so it can use additional space that has been added to its underlying storage

     Command : xfs_growfs

     Example : xfs_growfs /devops-data


24 . resize2fs resizes an EXT2/EXT3/EXT4 filesystem to use the additional space available on its  underlying device.

     Command : resize2fs

     Example : resize2fs /dev/ext4-vg/ext4-lv



  